## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to architect scalable, secure data ingestion across accounts with governance at scale, matching enterprise needs from Databricks and Salesforce.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-account IAM roles and resource policies
- Lake Formation governance and Glue Data Catalog
- Per-tenant S3 isolation and partitioning strategy
- KMS key management and envelope encryption
- Audit/logging with CloudTrail, Config, and Lake Formation logs

## Code Example

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject", "s3:PutObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-*-data-lake/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/tenant_id": "${aws:userid}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Interview Strategy

Focus on demonstrating enterprise-scale architecture patterns, emphasizing security isolation, governance automation, and cost optimization across multi-tenant environments.

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of cross-account temporary access, least-privilege IAM policies, and time-bound credentials using STS.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-account trust via AssumeRole
- Least privilege scoped to a specific S3 prefix
- Role duration controls expiry
- Testing access during and after the window

## Code Example
```json
// Trust policy (for the role in OUR account)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::PARTNER_ACCOUNT_ID:root"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
// Role policy (least privilege for PIX123)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::shared-docs",
      "Condition": {"StringLike": {"s3:prefix": ["contracts/PIX123/*"]}}
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::shared-docs/contracts/PIX123/*"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you revoke access before expiry if required?
- How would you audit the access and ensure logs show the temporary session usage?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses advanced AWS ABAC, cross-account governance, and policy-as-code in a multi-tenant data lake; targets practical use of IAM Identity Center, PrincipalTags, Lake Formation, and a GitOps deployment flow.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC with session/principal tags
- Lake Formation fine-grained permissions
- Cross-account policy deployment (GitOps)
- Revocation latency and audits (CloudTrail, Config, Access Analyzer)

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": { "Federated": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:saml-provider/AWS_SSO" },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "tenant-A"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject", "s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake",
        "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake/tenant-A/*"
      ],
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": { "s3:prefix": "tenant-A/" }
